[32m╭─ Claude ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│[39m **Dish: Chicken Biryani for 6**                                                                  [32m│
│[39m                                                                                                  [32m│
│[39m **Shopping list (added):**                                                                       [32m│
│[39m - Chicken, bone-in curry cut, 1.2 kg                                                             [32m│
│[39m - Ghee, 100 g                                                                                    [32m│
│[39m - Fresh mint and coriander, 1 bunch each                                                         [32m│
│[39m - Whole spices: cardamom, cloves, cinnamon, bay leaves                                           [32m│
│[39m - Red chilli powder                                                                              [32m│
│[39m - Lemons, 2                                                                                      [32m│
│[39m                                                                                                  [32m│
│[39m **Already in your pantry:** rice, onions, tomatoes, curd, ginger, garlic, green chillies,        [32m│
│[39m turmeric, cumin seeds, garam masala, oil and salt.                                               [32m│
│[39m                                                                                                  [32m│
│[39m **Steps:**                                                                                       [32m│
│[39m 1. **Marinate:** Mix the chicken with curd, ginger-garlic paste, chilli powder, turmeric, garam  [32m│
│[39m masala, lemon juice, salt and half the mint and coriander. Rest it for at least 1 hour.          [32m│
│[39m 2. **Fry onions:** Slice 4 onions and fry them in oil and ghee until deep golden. Set half aside [32m│
│[39m for layering.                                                                                    [32m│
│[39m 3. **Cook the chicken:** Cook the marinated chicken with the tomatoes and the remaining onions   [32m│
│[39m for 15 to 20 minutes, until it's about 80% done.                                                 [32m│
│[39m 4. **Parboil the rice:** Boil the soaked rice with whole spices and salt until it's 70% cooked,  [32m│
│[39m then drain.                                                                                      [32m│
│[39m 5. **Layer and steam:** Layer the rice over the chicken. Top with fried onions, herbs and ghee.  [32m│
│[39m Seal the pot and steam on the lowest heat for 20 to 25 minutes.                                  [32m│
│[39m                                                                                                  [32m│
│[39m **Note:** Your pantry just says "rice". Biryani works best with basmati, so check what you have. [32m│
│[39m If it isn't basmati, add some to the list. For 6 people you'll need about 600 to 700 g, and you  [32m│
│[39m have plenty.                                                                                     [32m│
